// Dev configuration for the iosApp target. Safe to commit with the defaults
// below: a blank HOROLOGIA_DEV_TOKEN forces the app into its Error state
// until a real token is supplied locally.
//
// To run locally against a dev server:
//   1. `mise run dev` from the repo root.
//   2. Mint a bearer token: log in as admin (`admin@localhost` / `password`)
//      and call POST /api/auth/tokens, then copy the token into
//      HOROLOGIA_DEV_TOKEN below.
//   3. Re-run `mise run //mobile:ios:build` or Cmd-R from Xcode.
//
// This file is tracked in git — do NOT commit a real token. If you need to
// share a value persistently, set it via an environment override on the
// xcodebuild invocation rather than editing this file.
//
// Note: xcconfig treats `//` as a line-comment start, so the scheme-slashes
// in the URL must straddle a `$()` expansion marker — at parse time it
// splits the `//` across two tokens, and at build-setting-expansion time
// `$()` evaluates to empty, leaving `http://localhost:8080/api/`.
//
// TODO: Remove once real auth flow is implemented —
//   POST /app/auth/login → cookie session → POST /api/auth/tokens (bearer token).

HOROLOGIA_BASE_URL = http:/$()/localhost:8080/api/
HOROLOGIA_DEV_TOKEN =
